---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { allPapers, OCR_MATERIALS, seriesRank } from '../../lib/data';
const exams = allPapers.filter((p) => p.kind === 'exam');
const seriesList = [...new Set(exams.map((p) => p.series))].sort((a, b) => seriesRank(b) - seriesRank(a));
const cell = (series, n) => exams.find((p) => p.series === series && p.paperNo === n);
const specimens = allPapers.filter((p) => p.kind === 'specimen');
---
<Base title="AQA A-level Law 7162 past papers 2020–2025, question by question" description="Every public AQA A-level Law (7162) paper: June 2022 to June 2025 and the November 2020 and 2021 series, Papers 1, 2, 3A and 3B, each with a question-by-question table, mark schemes and examiners' report comments." context="past-papers">
  <h1>AQA A-level Law past papers</h1>
  <p>Every AQA A-level Law (7162) paper that AQA has published: June 2022 to June 2025, the November 2020 and November 2021 series, and the specimen papers. Each paper page lists every question with its topic, marks, assessment objectives and type, and shows the questions with the mark scheme and the examiners' report.</p>
  <p><a class="btn" href={OCR_MATERIALS} rel="noopener">The papers on AQA's site</a></p>
  <div class="table-wrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Series</th><th>Paper 1</th><th>Paper 2</th><th>Paper 3A</th><th>Paper 3B</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{seriesList.map((s) => <tr><td>{s}</td>{['1', '2', '3A', '3B'].map((n) => { const p = cell(s, n); return <td>{p ? <a href={`/past-papers/${p.slug}/`}>{p.spec}/{p.comp}</a> : '—'}</td>; })}</tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Paper 1</strong> Criminal law, <strong>Paper 2</strong> Tort, and either <strong>Paper 3A</strong> Law of contract or <strong>Paper 3B</strong> Human rights. Each is 100 marks in 2 hours and a third of the A-level, and each also carries 25 marks on the nature of law and the English legal system.</li>
    <li>Every paper has the same eleven compulsory questions: five multiple-choice questions (1 mark each), two 5-mark questions, a 10-mark problem, a 15-mark essay and two 30-mark problems.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Specimen papers</h2>
  <p>{specimens.map((p, i) => <>{i ? ' · ' : ''}<a href={`/past-papers/${p.slug}/`}>{p.paper}: {p.name}</a></>)}</p>
  <h2>Gaps</h2>
  <ul class="muted">
    <li>The November 2020 and November 2021 series were sat on the papers printed for the cancelled summer exams, so their covers say June. AQA published no examiners' report for them or for the specimens: those questions have the mark scheme only.</li>
    <li>June 2019, the first exam, is no longer on AQA's site. The June 2026 papers will be added when AQA releases them, usually the following summer.</li>
    <li>Papers 3A and 3B print the same Questions 3 to 6. Both paper pages show them; topic pages and practice show them once.</li>
  </ul>
</Base>
